what is in the upstream zip.

## Intentional omissions

The upstream `sponza.zip` also contains **approximately 70 PNG
textures** under `textures/` totaling ~50 MiB. These are **not
vendored** because our matcher's `.kd`-only policy (see
`matcher_proposal §3.4` + `mesh.hpp:Material`) does not consume
`map_Kd` texture references — the matcher reads the scalar `Kd`
value directly from the MTL. The consequence for Sponza specifically
is documented in `research/scale_tier4_proposal.md` §1.6 and §1.8:
all 25 materials have identical `Kd = (1, 1, 1)`, so the entire mesh
voxelises to a single block (`minecraft:white_stained_glass`) under
the current matcher. Adding texture-sampling to the matcher is
deferred to v0.2 work item #4 (matcher quality); see
`OPEN_QUESTIONS.md` 2026-07-04 "Near-white opaque-branch matcher-
quality".

The `banner.obj` file mentioned in `copyright.txt` (the "long
untextured banner floating in the middle of the atrium" that McGuire
removed and split out into a separate file) is also **not vendored**;
it is not needed for the scale Tier-4 and is not part of the
canonical Crytek Sponza mesh under test.

## Re-fetching

To re-fetch and verify SHAs match this record:

    curl -fsSL --max-time 300 -o /tmp/sponza.zip \
        "https://casual-effects.com/g3d/data10/common/model/crytek_sponza/sponza.zip"
    sha256sum /tmp/sponza.zip  # expect da005cbe...2770c
    unzip /tmp/sponza.zip sponza.obj sponza.mtl copyright.txt -d /tmp/
    sha256sum /tmp/sponza.obj        # expect dc9d77fa...2493
    sha256sum /tmp/sponza.mtl        # expect 7e5d765a...9d9b
    sha256sum /tmp/copyright.txt     # expect 59967ef9...b70f6

If any SHA differs, the upstream has been updated since 2026-07-04
and the project must re-validate. The expectation per upstream
stability is that these files have been stable since 2011-07-14
(sponza.obj/copyright.txt mtime in the upstream zip; sponza.mtl mtime
2019-05-03 reflects a later minor edit that the community treats as
canonical).
